---
/**
 * Privacy policy — English mirror of src/pages/politique-de-confidentialite.astro.
 * Describes processing as actually implemented (checked in functions/api/*,
 * functions/lib/*, src/scripts/consent.ts, BaseLayout.astro). Application
 * retention periods and legal bases come from the WEBLACK TALENTS notice
 * written by the agency (Sanity, talentApplicationSettings). Keep both
 * languages in sync.
 */
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import { useTranslations, localizedPath } from "../../i18n/utils";
import { CONTACT_EMAIL } from "../../lib/contact";

const lang = "en" as const;
const t = useTranslations(lang);
const mail = `mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`;
---

<BaseLayout lang={lang} title={t("footer.privacy")} description={t("privacy.seo.description")}>
  <section class="bg-(--color-paper) px-6 pb-24 pt-40 md:px-10 md:pb-32">
    <div class="prose-weblack prose-weblack--ink mx-auto max-w-3xl">
      <h1 class="font-display text-4xl text-(--color-ink) sm:text-5xl">{t("footer.privacy")}</h1>
      <p class="text-sm text-(--color-ink)/60">
        Last updated: 21 October 2026 · <a href={localizedPath("fr", "/politique-de-confidentialite")} hreflang="fr" lang="fr">Version française</a> ·
        <a href="#google-user-data">Google user data</a>
      </p>

      <p>
        This policy explains what personal data the weblack.fr website and the WEBLACK TALENTS application collect, why,
        where it is stored, who can access it, how long it is kept and how to exercise your rights.
      </p>

      <h2>1. Data controller and contact</h2>
      <p>
        The data controller is the publisher of the WEBLACK website, a sole proprietorship (entreprise individuelle), whose
        identification, contact details and publication director are given in the
        <a href={localizedPath(lang, "/mentions-legales")}>legal notice</a>. For any question or
        request about your data: <a href={mail}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>2. Data collected and purposes</h2>

      <h3>2.1 Browsing the website</h3>
      <p>
        The website is hosted by Cloudflare (Cloudflare Pages). Like any host, Cloudflare processes the IP address and
        technical request information to deliver pages and protect the site against abuse. Editorial images are served by
        Sanity's content delivery network (cdn.sanity.io), which therefore receives the visitor's IP address. Fonts are
        hosted by the website itself.
      </p>

      <h3>2.2 Contact form</h3>
      <p>
        The contact form does not go through any server: it opens your own email client, pre-filled with your name, email
        address, organisation (optional), the profile you chose and your message. You send that message to
        {" "}{CONTACT_EMAIL} yourself. It is used only to answer your request and kept in WEBLACK's mailbox for as long as
        needed to handle it.
      </p>

      <h3>2.3 Newsletter</h3>
      <p>
        If you subscribe, your email address is added to the mailing list managed by our email provider Resend, based on
        your consent. It is used only to send you the newsletter; you can unsubscribe at any time, which ends the retention
        of your address for this purpose.
      </p>

      <h3>2.4 WEBLACK TALENTS applications</h3>
      <p>
        The <a href={localizedPath(lang, "/talent/candidature")}>application form</a>, open to people aged 18 and over only,
        collects:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>identity and contact details: first name, last name, date of birth, city, country, email, phone, Instagram (optional);</li>
        <li>professional profile: category, experience level and duration, portfolio links, current agency and exclusivity if any;</li>
        <li>measurements, all optional (height, chest, waist, hips, inseam, shoe size, clothing size, eye and hair colour);</li>
        <li>photographs: three required (portrait, profile, full-length dressed) and up to three additional ones; location metadata (EXIF) is removed before storage;</li>
        <li>languages, mobility, project types sought, optional introduction;</li>
        <li>confirmation that the information is accurate, the version of the privacy notice read, and the form language.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        Purposes: to receive and review the application, check that the person is an adult, get back to them and, where
        relevant, direct them to a suitable opportunity. The legal bases and retention policy specific to applications are
        detailed in the notice shown in step 5 of the form and summarised in sections 3 and 7 below. Submitting an
        application does not authorise publication of the photographs.
      </p>
      <p>
        Storage: the application is saved in a Cloudflare D1 database and the photographs in Cloudflare storage. A photo
        uploaded but never attached to an application (abandoned form) is deleted automatically after two hours. After
        submission, a confirmation email is sent to the applicant and an internal notification, with no name or contact
        details, is sent to the team, via Resend. An archive copy of the application may be filed in the agency's Google
        Drive (section 4).
      </p>
      <p>
        Access: applications and photographs are never public. They can only be viewed in the password-protected
        administration area, by authorised WEBLACK staff.
      </p>

      <h3>2.5 Security and abuse prevention</h3>
      <p>
        To limit automated submissions (form, photographs, administration sign-in), the number of requests per IP address
        is counted for one hour at most. The IP address is not stored in clear: only a truncated cryptographic hash is
        used, then erased when that period ends.
      </p>

      <h3>2.6 Cookies, local storage and analytics</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>
          Analytics: Google Analytics 4 is loaded only after your explicit consent, which you can withdraw at any time from
          "Privacy preferences" in the footer. Without consent, no data is sent to Google Analytics.
        </li>
        <li>
          Browser local storage (not cookies): your consent choice, your light/dark display preference and a marker that
          the newsletter pop-up has already been shown.
        </li>
        <li>
          Administration: a strictly necessary session cookie, only for authorised staff who sign in, valid for 12 hours
          and revoked on sign-out.
        </li>
        <li>
          Videos: the "Live" pages embed the YouTube player in privacy-enhanced mode (youtube-nocookie.com); Google
          (YouTube) may process data when you start playback.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>3. Legal bases</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Newsletter and analytics: your consent, which you can withdraw at any time.</li>
        <li>
          Applications (as set out in the WEBLACK TALENTS notice): pre-contractual steps taken at the applicant's request
          to review the application; WEBLACK's legitimate interest in running and securing the service; separate consent
          for any retention in a talent pool or any use of the photographs beyond the review; legal obligation or
          legitimate interest for the defence of rights.
        </li>
        <li>Website security and abuse prevention: WEBLACK's legitimate interest in protecting its services.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2 id="google-user-data">4. Google user data (Google Drive API)</h2>
      <p>
        The WEBLACK TALENTS application uses the Google Drive API to archive each application (a text summary and the
        photographs) in the Google Drive storage of the agency's account, {CONTACT_EMAIL}. Applicants never sign in with a
        Google account: only the agency's account authorises the application.
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          Google data accessed: only the folders and files the application has created itself (<code>drive.file</code>
          permission), and the email address of the authorising account (<code>openid</code> and <code>email</code>
          permissions), used once to check that it is the agency's account. The application has no access to any other
          file in the Drive.
        </li>
        <li>
          Use: create the <em>WEBLACK TALENTS / year / Candidatures / reference</em> folder structure, file the application
          there, check that it is present and that no public sharing link exists, and move it to the Google Drive trash
          when the application is deleted.
        </li>
        <li>
          Sharing: data obtained through Google APIs is not transferred to any third party, not sold, not used for
          advertising and not used to train artificial intelligence models.
        </li>
        <li>
          Storage and protection: the refresh token is kept only in the host's (Cloudflare) encrypted secrets, never in
          the code or in the browser; the access token only exists in memory for the duration of a request. The
          account's email address is not stored by the application: it is only compared, at authorisation time, with
          the expected address.
        </li>
        <li>
          Retention and deletion: archived files stay in the agency's Google Drive; the application keeps only their Drive
          identifiers (no content) in its database, for as long as the matching application. When the application is
          deleted, its identifiers are erased and the Drive folder is moved to the trash, which Google empties after 30
          days.
        </li>
        <li>
          Human access: only authorised WEBLACK staff view archived applications, to review them; no one else has access.
        </li>
        <li>
          Revocation: the agency can revoke access at any time from its Google account settings
          (myaccount.google.com/permissions); archiving then stops, with no effect on applications already saved. Any
          request about this data: <a href={mail}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        WEBLACK TALENTS's use and transfer of information received from Google APIs will adhere to the
        <a href="https://developers.google.com/terms/api-services-user-data-policy" rel="noopener">Google API Services User Data Policy</a>,
        including the Limited Use requirements.
      </p>

      <h2>5. Recipients and service providers</h2>
      <p>Data is accessible only to authorised WEBLACK staff. It is processed on WEBLACK's behalf, within the scope of their service, by:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Cloudflare: website hosting, server functions, application database, photograph storage;</li>
        <li>Resend: sending confirmation and notification emails, managing the newsletter list;</li>
        <li>Google: archiving applications in the agency's Google Drive; Google Analytics (only after consent); YouTube player;</li>
        <li>Sanity: editorial content management and delivery of website images. No application data is stored in Sanity.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>No data is sold or made public.</p>

      <h2>6. Transfers outside the European Union</h2>
      <p>
        The providers above may process data from countries outside the European Economic Area, including the United
        States. The applicable safeguards are those provided for in each provider's data protection terms.
      </p>

      <h2>7. Retention periods</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Unsuccessful applications: data and photographs deleted within three months at most after the application is closed, unless required by law.</li>
        <li>Talent pool: kept for two years at most from the last relevant contact, only where the applicant has been informed and the appropriate legal basis allows it.</li>
        <li>
          Deletion is carried out by the team in the administration area: it erases the application, its photographs and
          its pending emails; the matching Google Drive archive is moved to the trash, which Google empties automatically
          after 30 days.
        </li>
        <li>Photos uploaded but not attached to an application: deleted automatically after two hours.</li>
        <li>Abuse-prevention counters: one hour at most. Administration session: 12 hours at most.</li>
        <li>Newsletter: until you unsubscribe.</li>
        <li>Messages received through the contact form: as long as needed to handle the request.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>8. Security</h2>
      <p>
        Measures in place: encrypted connection (HTTPS) enforced; password-protected administration area with a signed,
        time-limited, revocable session; limits on repeated attempts; photographs served only to signed-in administrators,
        never through a public address; location data removed from photos; Google Drive permission limited to files
        created by the application; secrets kept only by the host. No measure guarantees zero risk.
      </p>

      <h2>9. Your rights</h2>
      <p>
        Under the General Data Protection Regulation (GDPR), you have the right of access, rectification, erasure,
        restriction, objection and, where applicable, portability, and the right to withdraw your consent at any time. To
        exercise them, write to <a href={mail}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>, giving the reference of your application if relevant.
        You may lodge a complaint with the French data protection authority, the CNIL
        (<a href="https://www.cnil.fr" rel="noopener">cnil.fr</a>).
      </p>

      <h2>10. Minors</h2>
      <p>WEBLACK TALENTS applications are open to people aged 18 and over only; an application from a minor is refused by the server.</p>

      <h2>11. Changes</h2>
      <p>This policy is updated when processing, providers or obligations change. The date of the last update is shown at the top of the page.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
